{"uid":"progs/src/lxabi.c::_GNU_SOURCE","name":"_GNU_SOURCE","qualname":"_GNU_SOURCE","kind":"macro","file":"progs/src/lxabi.c","line":17,"end_line":17,"language":"c","signature":"#define _GNU_SOURCE","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"lxabi.c - Linux process, thread and descriptor ABI probe (FreeDom readiness, docs/spec/smp-sched.md \"Linux process, thread and descriptor ABI\").","description":"A static glibc program that exercises exactly the kernel surface the full\nFreeDom GUI needs: register state across fork, clone threads with TLS and\njoin, auto-reaped detached threads, futex bitset waits with timeouts, pipe2\nand fcntl flags, blocking and non-blocking pipe I/O with EOF and EPIPE,\nclose-on-exit of a child's descriptors, writev into a pipe, eventfd, poll on\npipes and eventfds, close_range, time(2) and mkdir. Every check prints\n\"lxabi: <check> ok\" or \"lxabi: <check> FAIL <detail>\"; the run ends with\n\"lxabi: all ok\" and exit 0, or \"lxabi: <n> failed\" and exit 1.\n\nBuilt with -mno-red-zone: the register probe pushes onto the stack from\ninline assembly.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"progs/src/lxabi.c","members":[],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
